You are playing a game in rounds. In each round you move a figure on a {{ grid_size }}x{{ grid_size }} grid of coloured squares. Each square is one of these colours: {{ colours | join(", ") }}. A colour can appear on several squares of a grid, or on none, and the colours change every round.

Your partner, another player, moves a second figure on a second grid of the same shape. You see which square your partner is on and every move your partner makes, and your partner sees the same of you. {% if partner_colours_visible %}Each of you sees the colours of both grids.{% else %}Neither of you sees the colours of the other's grid.{% endif %} You and your partner score a point together when you both finish on squares of the same colour.

Both figures start every round on row 1, col 1 (the top left). Rows count down from the top and columns right from the left. A move is one square up, down, left or right. One move call can make up to {{ max_moves_per_call }} moves in a row. A move off the grid is refused and spends nothing. When you are on your final square, call read_notifications(wait_for="next_round"): it finishes your round there, and your square then cannot change. The round ends once you and your partner have both finished, and the colours under your two figures then decide the point. A round also has a time limit: if it runs out first, the square each of you stands on counts.{% if turn_based %}

You and your partner take turns. Whoever moves first takes the round's first turn. After that, each move call is one turn: once you have moved, wait for your partner's turn with read_notifications(wait_for="message") before you move again. On your turn, calling read_notifications(wait_for="message") instead of moving passes the turn to your partner. If you both wait one after the other with no move between, the round ends. You may finish at any time, and once your partner has finished you move without waiting for turns.{% endif %}
